  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Programme Monitoring for BOS Serbia 2016-2019</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Programsmonitoring BOS 2016-2019</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Monitoring for BOS Serbia programme 2016-2019</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="SV">Programesmonitoring BOS Serbien 2016-2019</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sida represented by the Embassy in Belgrade, Serbia&#xa0;entered into Agreement with the organisation Belgrade Open School (BOS) in Belgrade, with the purpose to finance through a grant the implementation of the proposed BOS programme for Serbia 2016-2020 &#x201c;CS4EU &#x2013; Civil Society as a Force for a Change in the Serbia&#x2019;s EU Accession Process&#x201d;&#xa0; (Contribution number 55100008). The Embassy decided to commission external Monitoring services to be continuously performed throughout the of the Project implementations, and to oversee all the tasks and metrics necessary to ensure that the approved Project is within scope, on time, and on budget so that the Project proceeds with minimal risk and that it maintains potential that its outcomes are delivered. This process involves comparing actual performance with planned performance and taking corrective action to yield the desired outcome when significant differences exist.</narrative>
  </description>
